# Frequency comparison across dimensions rejected

Verifies a comparison between a frequency and a duration is rejected at compile time. Kilohertz and seconds belong to separate dimensions, so no cross-dimensional comparison or scaling is available.

>>> source
frequency: int = 1khz
duration: int = 1s
print(frequency == duration)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: comparison `==` is not defined for `int64[khz]` and `int64[s]` at Span { start: 47, end: 68 }

<<< exit
1
